    q_{1} & -q_{1}  &  -q_1 & q_1 & q_2 & q_2 & -q_2 & -q_2
    \\\hline
  \end{tabular}
  \caption{A simple choice of charges for all fermions, leading
    to the low-energy effective action~(\ref{eq:97}). The charges are
    chosen in such a way that all gauge anomalies cancel. The cancellation of
    $U(1)_A^3$ and $U(1)_B^3$ anomalies happens for any value of
    $e_i,q_i$. Cancellation of mixed anomalies requires 
    $q_2=\displaystyle \frac{q_1(e_1^2-e_2^2)}{2(e_3^2-e_4^2)}$.} 
